  "term": "genetic monogamy",
  "definition": "Genetic monogamy is one end of the range of genetic mating-system patterns studied in animals, contrasted with polyandry. In the source, it is described as an alternative evolutionary strategy that has arisen multiple times under different ecological and biological conditions.",
